  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5169",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the relationship with NCI-H1155 through a multi-step mechanism involving P2X purinoceptors and a metabolite. The drug targets P2X purinoceptors 1 and 7, which are subsequently targeted by a metabolite of palmarumycin CP18. This metabolite, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, is known to act on P2X receptors and ultimately affects NCI-H1155. The evidence suggests that palmarumycin CP18 modulates the activity of these receptors, leading to a downstream effect on the target cell line. The final score of 0.5722 indicates a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, supported by the direct targeting of P2X receptors and the known target of the metabolite. The mechanism involves a chain of interactions where palmarumycin CP18 influences the activity of P2X receptors, which in turn affects NCI-H1155. This pathway highlights the importance of receptor-targeting in the therapeutic potential of palmarumycin CP18.",
